WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.370 --> 00:00:04.839
An intriguing character from Marvel comics
catalogue will be getting his very first solo

00:00:04.840 --> 00:00:09.200
movie vehicle in 2021: Shang-Chi, Master of
Kung Fu.

00:00:09.400 --> 00:00:13.550
Who is Shang-Chi, and how did he come to be
the master of kung-fu, and what is his place

00:00:13.550 --> 00:00:15.280
within the world of Marvel Comics?

00:00:15.280 --> 00:00:17.500
We're here to break down the details for you.

00:00:18.020 --> 00:00:21.900
You may be aware that in the early 1970s,
everybody was kung fu fighting.

00:00:22.020 --> 00:00:23.520
Or at least they wanted to be.

00:00:23.660 --> 00:00:28.040
This was largely thanks to Bruce Lee, who
had been exposed to American audiences via

00:00:28.040 --> 00:00:32.710
the television series The Green Hornet and
with starring roles in films including Game

00:00:32.710 --> 00:00:37.199
of Death and the posthumously-released Enter
the Dragon, which kicked open the door for

00:00:37.200 --> 00:00:39.380
future superstars like Jackie Chan.

00:00:39.510 --> 00:00:43.920
The TV series Kung Fu, which starred actor
David Carradine, is said to have originally

00:00:43.929 --> 00:00:45.750
been developed for Bruce Lee.

00:00:45.750 --> 00:00:49.260
Marvel hoped to adapt the series to cash in
on the martial arts craze.

00:00:49.260 --> 00:00:52.080
But the House of Ideas was unable to obtain
the rights...

00:00:52.340 --> 00:00:56.120
"As quickly as you can, snatch the pebble
from my hand."

00:01:01.680 --> 00:01:07.320
so then-Marvel Publisher Stan Lee turned to
creators Steve Englehart and Jim Starlin to

00:01:07.320 --> 00:01:09.760
come up with an original kung fu-based property.

00:01:09.970 --> 00:01:13.400
The character they created would go on to
become a Marvel mainstay.

00:01:13.410 --> 00:01:17.820
In the late '80s, long before Marvel came
to dominate the box office, Stan Lee attempted

00:01:17.820 --> 00:01:22.460
to get a Shang-Chi movie off the ground starring
Brandon Lee, Bruce's son.

00:01:22.460 --> 00:01:23.640
It never materialized.

00:01:24.340 --> 00:01:28.900
Not everyone was convinced that Master of
Kung Fu would be an instant hit, so Marvel

00:01:28.900 --> 00:01:33.480
introduced the character in a dead-end book
with the clunky title of Special Marvel Edition,

00:01:33.740 --> 00:01:38.410
which had up to that point published 14 issues
of reprints of older Marvel stories.

00:01:38.410 --> 00:01:43.230
Much like Spider-Man, who first appeared in
Amazing Fantasy #15, Shang-Chi debuted in

00:01:43.230 --> 00:01:47.960
the pages of Special Marvel Edition #15, published
in December 1973.

00:01:47.960 --> 00:01:49.020
The public quickly took notice.

00:01:49.060 --> 00:01:53.080
It took only two issues for the book's former
title to be dropped.

00:01:53.260 --> 00:01:57.700
It was renamed Hands of Shang-Chi: Master
of Kung Fu for the remainder of its run, which

00:01:57.700 --> 00:01:59.500
lasted until 1983.

00:01:59.600 --> 00:02:04.320
Shang-Chi enjoyed a respectable level of popularity
throughout the '70s, making guest appearances

00:02:04.320 --> 00:02:08.980
in several of Marvel's flagship books and
interacting with some of its most high-profile

00:02:08.980 --> 00:02:09.480
characters.

00:02:09.480 --> 00:02:13.940
Despite this success, it was, as they say,
a different time, and some elements of the

00:02:13.960 --> 00:02:16.440
character's backstory were more than a little
questionable.

00:02:17.300 --> 00:02:20.580
Chief among these problems was Shang-Chi's
lineage.

00:02:20.580 --> 00:02:25.530
In his very first appearance, he was presented
as the son of the evil Fu Manchu, an overtly

00:02:25.530 --> 00:02:30.140
racist supervillain who had appeared in pulp
novels and movies throughout the 20th Century.

00:02:30.460 --> 00:02:34.560
The character was among the most popular of
the so-called "Yellow Peril" villains, which

00:02:34.560 --> 00:02:39.409
spawned a number of devious, heartless Asian
evildoers such as Flash Gordon archvillain

00:02:39.409 --> 00:02:42.820
Ming the Merciless and the Batman villain
Ra's Al Ghul.

00:02:43.020 --> 00:02:47.780
Marvel obtained the rights from Fu Manchu's
creator, British novelist Sax Rohmer, and

00:02:47.790 --> 00:02:52.219
while their characterization was a touch more
dignified, many Asian readers nevertheless

00:02:52.220 --> 00:02:55.520
found the character to represent a demonization
of their culture.

00:02:55.680 --> 00:03:00.500
In his original origin, Shang-Chi was raised
by his father to be the ultimate assassin,

00:03:00.500 --> 00:03:03.200
but quickly came to reject Fu Manchu's evil
ways.

00:03:03.300 --> 00:03:05.740
Over the years, the two would clash repeatedly.

00:03:05.749 --> 00:03:10.090
In later years, the identity of the hero's
father would be retconned to actually be the

00:03:10.090 --> 00:03:16.080
immortal sorcerer Zheng Zhu, who for decades
had simply been using "Fu Manchu" as an alias.

00:03:16.100 --> 00:03:20.360
But this was largely due to the rights reverting
back to Rohmer's estate rather than a desire

00:03:20.360 --> 00:03:21.600
to rehab the character.

00:03:22.420 --> 00:03:26.640
Like many of Marvel's heroes, Shang-Chi technically
doesn't have any superpowers.

00:03:26.800 --> 00:03:31.420
He was molded by his father into the ultimate
weapon, a master practitioner of all forms

00:03:31.420 --> 00:03:32.840
of Chinese martial arts.

00:03:32.900 --> 00:03:37.020
Not only does this mean that he's an absurdly
skilled fighter, it also means that he has

00:03:37.020 --> 00:03:41.260
a level of control over his body that few
characters in the Marvel Universe can match.

00:03:41.360 --> 00:03:45.480
He's able to regulate a number of supposedly
involuntary bodily functions.

00:03:45.740 --> 00:03:49.540
For example, he can reduce the function of
his nerves to the extent that he's practically

00:03:49.540 --> 00:03:53.280
impervious to pain, and can even slow down
the rate at which he bleeds.

00:03:53.580 --> 00:03:57.930
He also has a master's knowledge of pressure
points, enabling him to take down opponents

00:03:57.930 --> 00:04:02.680
with a single strike, and is known to unleash
a bone-rattling flying kick which packs an

00:04:02.680 --> 00:04:04.400
unbelievable amount of force behind it.

00:04:04.540 --> 00:04:09.540
Like Captain America, he's said to represent
the peak of human strength, power and agility.

00:04:09.540 --> 00:04:14.700
He does, however, boast one skill specific
to only the most skilled of martial artists,

00:04:14.700 --> 00:04:19.700
one that raises his abilities to a level slightly
beyond those of fellow non-powered heroes.

00:04:20.320 --> 00:04:25.520
Shang-Chi has the ability to focus his chi,
the spiritual energy or "life force" inherent

00:04:25.540 --> 00:04:26.160
to all living things.

00:04:26.220 --> 00:04:30.860
In real-world martial arts, this practice
is used mainly in meditation and as a way

00:04:30.860 --> 00:04:32.741
of controlling one's fear and anger.

00:04:32.741 --> 00:04:36.830
In the Marvel universe, the ability can be
honed into a weapon, and Shang-Chi uses it

00:04:36.830 --> 00:04:39.380
to augment his skills to devastating effect.

00:04:39.560 --> 00:04:43.950
He can temporarily boost his strength and
endurance beyond even peak human levels, dodge

00:04:43.950 --> 00:04:48.009
or deflect bullets, and control his body's
reaction to poison or drugs.

00:04:48.009 --> 00:04:52.259
Because of these abilities and his utter mastery
of an array of deadly fighting styles, Shang-Chi

00:04:52.259 --> 00:04:56.941
is often considered to be the greatest unarmed
combatant in the entire Marvel universe; he

00:04:56.941 --> 00:05:01.629
was deemed by no less an authority than Black
Panther to be an even more formidable fighter

00:05:01.629 --> 00:05:03.680
than the superpowered Iron Fist.

00:05:03.700 --> 00:05:07.540
His mastery over his chi has even received
a technological boost.

00:05:07.620 --> 00:05:12.240
At times, he uses a special pair of nunchucks
designed by Tony Stark, which can accumulate

00:05:12.240 --> 00:05:16.860
and disperse Shang-Chi's spiritual energy,
unleashing deadly concussive blasts.

00:05:17.420 --> 00:05:21.480
Shang-Chi's interactions with other Marvel
heroes have been frequent, but one of his

00:05:21.480 --> 00:05:25.460
wilder team-ups was with an unlikely band
of New York-based heroes.

00:05:25.730 --> 00:05:29.240
It started with an investigation into the
bizarre slaughter of an entire faction of

00:05:29.250 --> 00:05:30.850
Brooklyn mafia members.

00:05:30.850 --> 00:05:36.389
Daredevil discovered it was the work of Ulik,
a rock troll hailing from Asgard's underworld

00:05:36.389 --> 00:05:38.860
who had come to Earth in search of a mystical
horn.

00:05:39.140 --> 00:05:43.919
Daredevil enlisted the aid of Shang-Chi, Black
Widow, a Cloak-less Dagger, and the Punisher

00:05:43.919 --> 00:05:47.820
to form the "Marvel Knights" and deal with
Ulik and his minions.

00:05:47.820 --> 00:05:51.780
Afterwards, the rest of the group became determined
to bring the Punisher — whose methods they

00:05:51.780 --> 00:05:54.160
found to be unsavory — to justice.

00:05:54.340 --> 00:05:58.599
They were joined in this dangerous endeavor
by Moon Knight, but the revamped group's efforts

00:05:58.599 --> 00:06:03.030
were interrupted by Cloak, who was in the
psychological clutches of the demon Nightmare

00:06:03.030 --> 00:06:05.980
and was on a misguided rampage to consume
all evildoers.

00:06:06.100 --> 00:06:10.960
After consuming the Punisher, Daredevil, Black
Widow, and Moon Knight, Cloak was halted by

00:06:10.970 --> 00:06:15.740
Doctor Strange, whom Dagger had brought in
to assist before things got truly out of hand.

00:06:15.740 --> 00:06:18.540
By the end of the series, the Punisher was
still punishing away.

00:06:19.380 --> 00:06:23.919
Shang-Chi has occasionally been called upon
to train other heroes in hand-to-hand combat,

00:06:23.920 --> 00:06:26.040
including your friendly neighborhood wall-crawler.

00:06:26.040 --> 00:06:30.680
During the "Revenge of the Spider-Slayer"
story arc, Spider-Man realized that the villain

00:06:30.689 --> 00:06:35.460
Alistair Smythe had found a way to imbue his
Spider-Slayer robots with a version of his

00:06:35.460 --> 00:06:36.420
spider-sense.

00:06:36.660 --> 00:06:41.639
He created a device to disrupt the ability,
but was forced to set it off manually, deactivating

00:06:41.640 --> 00:06:43.580
his own spider-sense in the process.

00:06:43.660 --> 00:06:48.040
This caused some difficulty in the subsequent
"Spider Island" event, during which thousands

00:06:48.040 --> 00:06:51.940
of heroes, villains, and ordinary citizens
alike developed spider-powers.

00:06:52.000 --> 00:06:55.480
On the recommendation of Madame Web, Spidey
went to Shang-Chi for training.

00:06:56.240 --> 00:07:01.120
He created a completely new martial arts style
intended to complement Spider-Man's powers,

00:07:01.120 --> 00:07:02.920
which he called "The Way of the Spider."

00:07:03.000 --> 00:07:07.900
Spider-Man became an even more dangerous fighter
than he already was, using his newfound martial

00:07:08.380 --> 00:07:13.600
arts prowess to take down opponents as powerful
and skilled as Spider-Woman and even Shang-Chi

00:07:13.680 --> 00:07:14.180
himself.

00:07:15.040 --> 00:07:18.640
Shang-Chi has at times been imparted with
superhuman abilities.

00:07:18.720 --> 00:07:22.980
During the aforementioned "Spider Island"
event, he was one of the many temporarily

00:07:22.980 --> 00:07:27.280
granted the same powers as Spider-Man, a scary
notion if ever there was one.

00:07:27.480 --> 00:07:31.340
He used these powers to help dispatch the
threat of the spider-powered supervillains

00:07:31.340 --> 00:07:33.400
running roughshod over New York City.

00:07:33.540 --> 00:07:38.400
In another incident, Shang-Chi was dispatched
with other Avengers to the fictional island

00:07:38.400 --> 00:07:43.270
of Madripoor to deal with an ancient dragon
which had been awakened from its slumber underneath

00:07:43.270 --> 00:07:43.780
the island.

00:07:44.000 --> 00:07:49.440
Using Pym Particles, Shang-Chi enlarged himself
to match the dragon's Godzilla-like stature,

00:07:49.440 --> 00:07:51.580
and promptly defeated it in combat.

00:07:51.669 --> 00:07:56.460
In a more recent incident, Shang-Chi volunteered
to investigate the city of Kobe, Japan after

00:07:56.470 --> 00:08:01.240
it was struck with the evolution-speeding
Origin Bomb by the godlike entity known as

00:08:01.240 --> 00:08:02.080
Ex Nihilo.

00:08:02.260 --> 00:08:07.120
While others had been absorbed by the "genesis
matter" which was a by-product of the bombing,

00:08:07.120 --> 00:08:10.689
Shang-Chi was able to commune with it, and
in the process gained the ability to produce

00:08:10.689 --> 00:08:15.200
an unknown number of duplicates of himself,
each one with the original's memories and

00:08:15.200 --> 00:08:15.700
abilities.

00:08:15.780 --> 00:08:18.300
It's unknown whether he still possesses this
power.

00:08:18.960 --> 00:08:23.380
Back in 2006, when Marvel first announced
its intention to start Marvel Studios and

00:08:23.389 --> 00:08:27.319
produce a slate of films featuring some of
its lesser-known characters, virtually no

00:08:27.319 --> 00:08:31.770
one was thinking that the endeavor would result
in the single highest-grossing film franchise

00:08:31.770 --> 00:08:32.580
of all time.

00:08:34.700 --> 00:08:35.500
"Avengers!

00:08:40.780 --> 00:08:41.780
Assemble."

00:08:41.900 --> 00:08:46.200
The rights to Marvel's most famous properties,
namely Spider-Man and the X-Men, were held

00:08:46.200 --> 00:08:51.040
by Sony and Fox respectively, both of which
had created successful film franchises.

00:08:51.040 --> 00:08:55.060
Marvel seemed to be coming late to the party,
with a stable of characters that included,

00:08:55.060 --> 00:08:59.910
in the order they were announced: Captain
America, The Avengers, Nick Fury, Black Panther,

00:08:59.910 --> 00:09:04.400
Ant-Man, Cloak &amp; Dagger, Doctor Strange, Hawkeye,
Power Pack, and Shang-Chi.

00:09:04.520 --> 00:09:08.520
Marvel Studios would, of course, go on to
elevate many of these properties to household

00:09:08.520 --> 00:09:12.620
name status, although some took considerably
longer to develop than others.

00:09:12.620 --> 00:09:17.060
Ant-Man took a full nine years to reach the
big screen, and the pre-teen Power Pack have

00:09:17.060 --> 00:09:19.079
yet to get its time in the spotlight.

00:09:19.079 --> 00:09:23.690
But finally, well over a decade after the
fact, Shang-Chi stands poised to join the

00:09:23.690 --> 00:09:28.150
MCU, thanks in part to another solo vehicle
which became one of Marvel's biggest success

00:09:28.150 --> 00:09:31.000
stories and one of the biggest films of 2018.

00:09:31.800 --> 00:09:33.720
Black Panther astonished audiences.

00:09:33.860 --> 00:09:38.480
Crafted mainly by African-American filmmakers
and featuring a hero who is the king of the

00:09:38.480 --> 00:09:41.120
technologically advanced African nation of
Wakanda...

00:09:41.780 --> 00:09:43.300
“This never gets old."

00:09:43.440 --> 00:09:48.290
the film proved that big-budget blockbusters
created from a specific cultural viewpoint

00:09:48.290 --> 00:09:52.760
can resonate strongly with general audiences,
and it even outgrossed the juggernaut that

00:09:52.760 --> 00:09:55.920
was Avengers: Infinity War at the domestic
box office.

00:09:56.080 --> 00:10:00.700
Taking a cue from this success, Marvel appears
to have gone all-in on diversity, and it's

00:10:00.700 --> 00:10:05.610
likely the studio's hope that Shang-Chi and
the Legend of the Ten Rings can strike a similar

00:10:05.610 --> 00:10:07.440
chord in pop culture at large.

00:10:07.660 --> 00:10:11.740
To this end, the production has been loaded
up with talented people of Asian descent on

00:10:11.740 --> 00:10:13.100
both sides of the camera.

00:10:13.220 --> 00:10:18.220
Japanese/Irish American Destin Daniel Cretton
will direct from a screenplay by Chinese-American

00:10:18.230 --> 00:10:22.880
scribe Dave Callaham, who is contributing
to Warner Brothers' upcoming Wonder Woman

00:10:22.880 --> 00:10:28.430
1984 as well as Sony Pictures Animation's
as-yet untitled sequel to Spider-Man: Into

00:10:28.430 --> 00:10:29.000
the Spider-Verse.

00:10:29.160 --> 00:10:34.380
Chinese-Canadian actor Simu Liu has landed
the title role, and the suddenly ubiquitous

00:10:34.400 --> 00:10:38.080
rapper-turned-actor Awkwafina will appear
among the supporting cast.

00:10:38.140 --> 00:10:43.300
Legendary Chinese actor Tony Leung will co-star
as the Mandarin, an iconic villain who many

00:10:43.300 --> 00:10:46.520
fans feel was previously given extremely short
shrift.

00:10:47.120 --> 00:10:51.560
The title of Shang-Chi's solo vehicle quickly
got the attention of Marvel fans, alluding

00:10:51.570 --> 00:10:56.839
as it does to a mysterious terrorist organization
that has lurked in the shadows of the MCU

00:10:56.840 --> 00:10:57.860
since its inception.

00:10:57.920 --> 00:11:02.279
The Ten Rings are the group responsible for
Tony Stark's kidnapping in Iron Man, they've

00:11:02.280 --> 00:11:06.140
been alluded to in both of that film's sequels
as well as Ant-Man.

00:11:06.340 --> 00:11:11.300
They're led by none other than the real Mandarin,
who famously a ring on every finger in the

00:11:11.300 --> 00:11:11.800
comics.

00:11:11.880 --> 00:11:16.780
This is not the phony Trevor Slattery or his
handler Aldrich Killian, both of whom falsely

00:11:16.780 --> 00:11:18.600
laid claim to the Mandarin name.

00:11:18.900 --> 00:11:19.900
"Where's the Mandarin?

00:11:19.900 --> 00:11:20.600
Where is he?"

00:11:20.600 --> 00:11:21.100
"Whoa!

00:11:21.100 --> 00:11:21.940
Whoa whoa whoa whoa whoa!

00:11:21.940 --> 00:11:22.440
He's here.

00:11:22.440 --> 00:11:24.460
He's here, but he's not here.

00:11:24.460 --> 00:11:25.460
He's here but he's not here."

00:11:25.480 --> 00:11:30.420
In Shang-Chi and the Legend of the Ten Rings,
this group will finally step out of the shadows

00:11:30.420 --> 00:11:32.280
and truly make their presence felt.

00:11:32.440 --> 00:11:37.120
The Ten Rings are dedicated to nothing less
than the destabilization of the entire planet,

00:11:37.120 --> 00:11:40.860
sowing the kind of chaos which will lead to
the collapse of world governments and create

00:11:40.860 --> 00:11:41.680
a power vacuum.

00:11:42.110 --> 00:11:45.880
They've butted heads with Iron Man, Black
Widow, and Nick Fury, but they'll soon face

00:11:45.900 --> 00:11:50.240
the Master of Kung-Fu, who never met a challenge
that he couldn't kick the absolute crap out

00:11:50.240 --> 00:11:50.740
of.

00:11:51.260 --> 00:11:53.160
Check out one of our newest videos right here!

00:11:53.350 --> 00:11:56.180
Plus, even more Looper videos about the MCU
are coming soon.

00:11:56.199 --> 00:11:59.410
Subscribe to our YouTube channel and hit the
bell so you don't miss a single one.

